var e=`July 21 • July 28 • August 4 • August 11`,t=`Śrāvaṇa Mangalavāra = Day of Pārvatī as Mangala Gaurī — Giver of Marriage + Suhāga + Santāna`,n=`Śrāvaṇa Mangalavāra is traditionally dedicated to Mangala Gaurī, a form of Goddess Pārvatī associated with auspiciousness, marital harmony, family well-being and devotion. Devotees observe the Mangala Gaurī Vratam with Ārādhana, Abhiṣeka and Archana through the sacred Tuesdays of Śrāvaṇa.`,r=[{num:`01`,title:`Pārvatī’s Vrat`,source:`Bhaviṣya Purāṇa`,text:`The tradition of Mangala Gaurī Vratam is associated with Pārvatī’s devotion and tapas for Śiva. Śrāvaṇa Tuesdays are therefore regarded as especially auspicious for Gaurī worship.`},{num:`02`,title:`Mangala = Mars Day`,source:`Skanda Purāṇa`,text:`Tuesday is traditionally associated with Mangala / Mars. Devotees perform Gaurī worship seeking harmony, courage and removal of obstacles connected with marriage and family life.`},{num:`03`,title:`Saubhāgya Śakti`,source:`Devī Bhāgavata`,text:`Mangala Gaurī represents an auspicious form of Pārvatī associated with saubhāgya, marital harmony and family well-being.`},{num:`04`,title:`Cāturmāsya`,source:`Padma Purāṇa`,text:`Śrāvaṇa falls within the sacred Cāturmāsya period, traditionally encouraging increased devotion, vrata, prayer and dāna.`},{num:`05`,title:`Red Color Energy`,source:`Traditional Teaching`,text:`Red is traditionally associated with auspiciousness, feminine divine energy and the Sumaṅgalī tradition. Devotees may therefore use red clothing, bangles and kumkum as part of traditional worship.`}],i={heading:`Tantra Śāstra Reason`,body:`Traditional Śākta and Śaiva practices associate Tuesday with Mangala and fiery energy. Mangala Gaurī worship symbolically invokes Pārvatī’s auspicious and nurturing power. Turmeric and kumkum are traditionally important substances in Gaurī worship and are associated with purity, auspiciousness and feminine divine energy.`},a=`Traditional Śrāvaṇa Māhātmya traditions associate Mangala Gaurī Vratam with prayers for:`,o=[{num:`01`,title:`Kanya`,text:`Unmarried devotees pray for a suitable, righteous and harmonious marriage.`},{num:`02`,title:`Suhāgan`,text:`Married women traditionally observe the vrata seeking marital harmony, family well-being and the long life and welfare of their husbands.`},{num:`03`,title:`Santāna`,text:`Couples traditionally pray for children and family prosperity.`},{num:`04`,title:`Griha Śānti`,text:`Devotees pray for peace and harmony between family members.`},{num:`05`,title:`Mangal Doṣa Śānti`,text:`Some traditions associate Mangala Gaurī worship with prayers for overcoming marriage-related obstacles and perceived Mangala Doṣa.`}],s={transliteration:`“Śrāvaṇe maṅgalavāre gaurīṁ pūjayate tu yaḥ | Saubhāgyaṁ putra-pautraṁ ca labhate nātra saṁśayaḥ ||”`,meaning:`One who worships Gaurī on Śrāvaṇa Tuesday is traditionally praised as receiving saubhāgya, family prosperity and blessings for future generations.`},c=`Abhiṣeka is the devotional practice of bathing the deity with sacred substances known as dravyas. In Mangala Gaurī worship the offering is made with auspicious, purifying substances according to tradition.`,l=[{num:`01`,name:`Turmeric Water`,detail:`Traditionally associated with auspiciousness, purification and Mangala Gaurī worship.`},{num:`02`,name:`Milk`,detail:`Traditionally associated with purity, nourishment, peace and family well-being.`},{num:`03`,name:`Coconut Water`,detail:`Traditionally associated with fertility, nourishment and family blessings.`},{num:`04`,name:`Kumkum Water`,detail:`Associated with saubhāgya, auspiciousness and the divine feminine.`},{num:`05`,name:`Sugar + Honey`,detail:`Traditionally associated with sweetness, harmonious speech and peaceful relationships.`},{num:`06`,name:`Pañcamṛta`,detail:`A traditional sacred offering representing nourishment and auspiciousness.`},{num:`07`,name:`Rose Water`,detail:`Traditionally associated with love, beauty, devotion and heart-centered worship.`},{num:`08`,name:`Bilva Leaf Water`,detail:`Bilva is sacred in Śiva worship and represents the divine connection between Śiva and Pārvatī.`},{num:`09`,name:`16 Śṛṅgāra Items`,detail:`Traditional Solah Śṛṅgāra offerings may include auspicious adornments offered to Gaurī according to family and temple tradition.`}],u=[{num:`01`,name:`Vivāha Siddhi`,text:`Prayer for a suitable, harmonious and dharmic marriage.`},{num:`02`,name:`Saubhāgya Vṛddhi`,text:`Prayer for marital happiness, mutual respect and family welfare.`},{num:`03`,name:`Santāna Sukha`,text:`Traditional prayers for children and family well-being.`},{num:`04`,name:`Mangal Doṣa Śānti`,text:`Traditional devotional practice for those seeking spiritual remedies for perceived marriage-related planetary obstacles.`},{num:`05`,name:`Griha Lakṣmī`,text:`Prayer for prosperity, nourishment and abundance within the household.`},{num:`06`,name:`Śānti`,text:`Prayer for harmony and resolution of family conflicts.`},{num:`07`,name:`Saundarya`,text:`Traditional worship associated with beauty, confidence, grace and inner radiance.`},{num:`08`,name:`Mokṣa`,text:`The ultimate purpose of devotion is spiritual growth, surrender and liberation.`}],d=`These benefits are presented as traditional devotional beliefs and spiritual aspirations, not guaranteed outcomes.`,f={heading:`Tantra Practice`,body:`Traditional practices may include Archana with 108 names and devotional use of a red thread according to one’s family, guru or sampradāya tradition. Do not present ritual practices as guaranteed supernatural results.`},p=[{step:1,title:`Preparation`,points:[`Observe an appropriate fast according to personal health and family tradition.`,`Wear clean traditional clothing, traditionally red or yellow where appropriate.`,`Prepare a Gaurī image or idol according to your tradition.`]},{step:2,title:`Abhiṣeka — 11 Minutes`,points:[`Offer: Turmeric water → Milk → Rose water → Clean water.`,`Recite the appropriate Gaurī mantra according to one’s guru or sampradāya.`]},{step:3,title:`Archana — 16 Minutes`,points:[`Offer traditional auspicious items such as kumkum, turmeric, bangles, bindi, toe rings, saree, mirror, comb and other traditional Śṛṅgāra items.`,`Recite the Gaurī Aṣṭottara or Lalitā Sahasranāma according to one’s tradition.`]},{step:4,title:`Kathā + Prārthanā — 10 Minutes`,points:[`Read the Mangala Gaurī Vrat Katha.`,`Traditional prayers may include: Patim Dehi • Putram Dehi • Saubhāgyam Dehi.`]},{step:5,title:`Dāna + Udyāpana — 8 Minutes`,points:[`Offer suitable traditional gifts such as red bangles, saree, turmeric and kumkum to married women according to one’s family tradition.`]}],m=[{num:`01`,name:`Red`,text:`Red bangles, bindi and other auspicious adornments are traditionally associated with Mangala Gaurī worship.`},{num:`02`,name:`Personal Discipline`,text:`Maintain cleanliness, simplicity and devotional discipline.`},{num:`03`,name:`16 Offerings`,text:`Traditional Gaurī worship may emphasize groups of sixteen auspicious offerings.`},{num:`04`,name:`Fasting`,text:`Those observing a fast may follow the food restrictions prescribed by their family or sampradāya.`},{num:`05`,name:`Śrāvaṇa Tuesdays`,text:`Devotees may observe the practice across the Śrāvaṇa Tuesdays according to their family tradition.`}],h=[{label:`Purāṇa`,text:`Śrāvaṇa Tuesday is traditionally regarded as an auspicious day for Pārvatī / Mangala Gaurī worship.`},{label:`Tantra`,text:`Traditional Śākta practices emphasize turmeric, kumkum, Archana, mantra and devotional discipline.`},{label:`Result`,text:`The deeper purpose of Mangala Gaurī Vratam is devotion, marital harmony, family well-being, auspiciousness and spiritual growth.`}],g=`“Mangala Gaurī doesn’t just give a husband. She blesses the seeker with a dharmic marriage rooted in devotion, harmony and lasting family happiness.”`,_=`This is a devotional/editorial message rather than a direct scriptural quotation.`,v=[`Bhaviṣya Purāṇa`,`Skanda Purāṇa`,`Devī Bhāgavata`,`Padma Purāṇa`,`Śāradā Tilaka Tantra`,`Śrāvaṇa Māhātmya Traditions`];export{i as _,h as a,_ as c,r as d,m as f,f as g,t as h,d as i,n as l,v as m,l as n,e as o,s as p,u as r,g as s,c as t,p as u,a as v,o as y};